<%- include('../partials/layout-start') %>
<%- include('../partials/page-header', { icon: 'bi-file-text', heading: 'Terms of service' }) %>
<section class="glass-section pb-5">
<div class="container">
  <div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-8">
    <div class="glass-card"><div class="card-body legal-doc">
      <p class="text-muted-2">Version <%= version %></p>

      <%#
        Every fact here that can change — the operator, the law, the age, the notice period,
        the support address — is read from config/legalEntity.js or the app config, never
        typed into this page. A promise this page makes is one the code keeps: closure is
        AccountClosure, the reporting route is /report-issue, the notice to an author is
        Moderation's. Change the behaviour and this text with it, and bump TERMS_VERSION.
      -%>

      <h2 class="h6">1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>SAP Hub (the "service") is operated by <strong><%= entity.name %></strong><% if (entity.registrationNumber) { %>,
         registration number <%= entity.registrationNumber %><% } %><% if (entity.address) { %>,
         <%= entity.address %><% } %>. You can reach us at
         <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> or through the
         <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. These terms are an agreement between you and
         <%= entity.name %>.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">2. Who may use the service</h2>
      <p>You must be at least <%= entity.minimumAge %> years old to create an account. If you use the
         service on behalf of a company, you confirm that you are allowed to act for it, and these
         terms bind that company as well as you.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">3. The service</h2>
      <p>SAP Hub connects consultants and companies in the SAP ecosystem. We are a marketplace: we
         are not party to any engagement agreed through it, and we do not employ, vet or guarantee
         anyone listed here. Estimates, benchmarks and the rate index are information, not advice.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">4. Your account</h2>
      <p>One account per person. Keep your password to yourself. You are responsible for what is
         posted from your account and for keeping the details on it accurate.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">5. What you post, and the licence you give us</h2>
      <p>Job adverts and profiles must be truthful and must describe a real role or a real person.
         Discriminatory adverts, fake listings and content copied from elsewhere without permission
         are not allowed.</p>
      <p>You keep ownership of what you post. By posting it you give <%= entity.name %> a
         non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide licence to host, store, display and distribute it
         on the service, for as long as it is on the service and as needed to operate it. For your
         profile this follows your own settings: a profile is shown only when you publish it, and
         your name and photograph are shown only to signed-in members.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">6. Rate contributions</h2>
      <p>Contribute your own figures only. By contributing you allow us to use the figure,
         anonymously, in the rate index. It is never shown with your name, and a figure is
         published only as part of a group of at least <%= rateMinSample %> people. The index is a
         community estimate, not advice and not a guarantee of what anyone will pay.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">7. What you may not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>scrape, crawl or harvest the service, or copy its listings, profiles or rate data in
            bulk, by automated means or otherwise, except through features we provide for that;</li>
        <li>use the service, or anything taken from it, to send unsolicited messages;</li>
        <li>impersonate anybody, or hold more than one account;</li>
        <li>try to get around a limit, a block or a security measure;</li>
        <li>post anything unlawful, or anything that infringes somebody else's rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h6">8. Reporting content</h2>
      <p>If you think something on the service is unlawful or breaks these terms, report it through
         the <a href="/report-issue">Report Issue</a> page (choose "Abuse") or write to
         <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>, which is also our single point
         of contact for authorities and users under the EU Digital Services Act. Tell us where it is
         and why you think it should come down. A person reviews every report.</p>
      <p>When we remove a post, a reply, a profile or a job advert from public view, we tell its
         author what was removed and why, and they can ask us to look again by writing to us. We
         hide content rather than delete it, so a decision we reverse is restored as it was.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">9. Suspension and closing an account</h2>
      <p><strong>You</strong> can close your account at any time from
         <a href="/profile/settings/close">Account settings → Close account</a>. Closing it erases your
         name, email address, password, profiles and photograph. Some records stay, because they
         belong to other people or to our books:</p>
      <ul>
        <% closureKept.forEach(function (k) { %>
          <li><strong><%= k.what %>.</strong> <%= k.why %></li>
        <% }) %>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>We</strong> may remove content, or suspend or close an account, if it breaks these
         terms or the law, or to protect other users. We tell the account holder which, and why,
         unless the law prevents us or the account was plainly created to abuse the service. A
         suspended account can ask us to look again. What happens to personal data is described in
         the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">10. Payments</h2>
      <p>Paid features — today a featured placement for a job advert and a deposit against an
         accepted estimate — show their price before you pay. Payments are processed by Stripe; we
         never see or store your card details. An invoice is issued for each payment and can be found
         under Payments in your account.</p>
      <p>A featured placement starts when it is paid and is not refundable once it has started,
         except where the law says otherwise. A deposit is credited against the engagement it was
         paid for. If you were charged in error or twice, write to us and we will refund it.
         <% if (!paymentsReady) { %>Card payments are not switched on yet; nothing on the service can
         charge you until they are.<% } %></p>

      <h2 class="h6">11. Privacy</h2>
      <p>How we collect and use personal data — including profiles and the salary and rate figures
         you give us — is described in the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy policy</a>, which forms
         part of these terms.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">12. Trademarks</h2>
      <p>SAP, S/4HANA, SuccessFactors, Ariba, Concur, Fieldglass and related names are
         trademarks of SAP SE. This service is independent and not affiliated with,
         endorsed by, or sponsored by SAP SE.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">13. Liability</h2>
      <p>The service is provided as it is. To the extent permitted by law, <%= entity.name %> is not
         liable for engagements agreed through the service, for hiring decisions, or for losses
         arising from information found here. Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or
         personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, for gross negligence or wilful misconduct,
         or any other liability that cannot be limited by law, and nothing affects rights you have
         as a consumer that cannot be waived.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">14. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>The version at the top of this page is the date of the current text. When we change these
         terms materially we will tell you by email or by a notice on the service at least
         <%= entity.noticeDays %> days before the change takes effect. If you continue to use the
         service after that date, the new terms apply; if you do not agree, you can close your
         account before then.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">15. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by <%= entity.governingLaw %>. Disputes are decided by
         <%= entity.courts %>, unless the law of the country you live in gives you, as a consumer,
         the right to bring or defend a claim in your own courts.</p>
    </div></div>
  </div></div>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/layout-end') %>
